abstract: >
  Python implementation and reproducibility material for the numerical
  validation of kinetic derivative observability and constructive curvature
  reconstruction in D2Q9, D3Q15, D3Q19, and D3Q27 lattice Boltzmann models.
  The repository archives the exact normalized CE2 observability operators
  for D3Q15, D3Q19, and D3Q27, the lattice-specific Hermite curvature
  reconstruction operators and their observable functional definitions, and
  the numerical experiments supporting the associated Physics of Fluids
  manuscript: finite-wavenumber D2Q9 shear-mode validation,
  three-dimensional D3Q19/D3Q27 CE2 population-response calculations, a
  weakly nonlinear Taylor-Green cross-check, and curvature reconstruction
  from exact linearized and fully evolved BGK shear modes (Experiment IV).

